title: Anubis/Lindnor - Masqueraded Service Binary or Ransom Note Creation
id: 8f4f2c1e-5b7a-4f0d-9a2b-6c1d3e8b7a54
status: experimental
description: Detects file creation of the Lindnor backdoor binaries Symantec documented masquerading as a Chrome component (healthcontroller64.exe) and a VMware file (svchelper.exe) on Microsoft SQL Server hosts, and of the Anubis encryption payload's ransom notes (restore files.txt / restore files.html). Derived from case analysis (Symantec) - NOT validated against a live sample.
references:
  - https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/lindnor-new-backdoor-anubis-ransomware
  - https://securityonline.info/lindnor-backdoor-anubis-ransomware-byovd/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-11-09
tags:
  - attack.t1036
  - attack.t1543
  - attack.t1486
logsource:
  category: file_event
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_masquerade:
    TargetFilename|endswith:
      - '\healthcontroller64.exe'
      - '\svchelper.exe'
  selection_ransom_note:
    TargetFilename|endswith:
      - '\restore files.txt'
      - '\restore files.html'
  condition: selection_masquerade or selection_ransom_note
falsepositives:
  - Backup or recovery tooling that writes a file literally named "restore files.txt" or "restore files.html"
  - An unrelated software package shipping a binary named healthcontroller64.exe or svchelper.exe
level: high
